---
description: Use Archi-Made-Easy for plain-language architecture and diagram requests (design, draw, explain, repository-to-diagram, requirements-to-architecture).
alwaysApply: false
---

For architecture and diagram requests, follow `archi-made-easy/SKILL.md`. It is the single source of truth.

- Read `archi-made-easy/references/intents.md` for requests beyond "draw X".
- The user speaks plain language. You author the JSON candidate and run `node archi-made-easy/bin/archi-made-easy.mjs finalize <type> <candidate.json> <output.html> --quality showcase --json`.
- Ask at most three material questions, each with a default. List every assumption.
- Never present invented numbers as real. Review, simulation and cost analysis are not in this version.
- A non-zero exit from `finalize` is never success.
